sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: The data flow of a search
    accDescr: A user searches for invoice. The unified search passes the term, the cursor, the limit, the date filter and the user to the search provider. Without a term, an archive account or a connection, the provider answers with no results and doesn't ask Paperless. Otherwise, until the page of results is full, the Paperless client asks Paperless-ngx with the token for the page of 25 hits that holds the next hit, within the days of the date filter, and only for the fields that a result shows, and Paperless answers with the ID, the title, the date, the IDs of the correspondent and the type and the excerpt of documents 412, 389, 371 and more, and whether a next page exists. One call of the file locator covers all documents of that page and returns for each a file of the archive account with its marker, or none. For the documents with a file, the names ask Paperless, through the client, for the correspondents and the types that the cache doesn't hold, with one request per kind, and keep their names for ten minutes. This repeats for at most 4 pages of Paperless or 3 seconds. The provider answers with an entry for every document with a file, up to the limit, with the preview of the file or the icon of its type, the title, the date in the language of the user, the correspondent, the type and the excerpt, and the cursor of the first hit that it didn't go through.

    actor User
    participant Search as Unified search
    participant Provider as Search provider
    participant Client as Paperless client
    participant Paperless as Paperless-ngx
    participant Locator as File locator
    participant Names as Names
    User->>Search: invoice
    Search->>Provider: term, cursor, limit,<br>date filter and user
    alt no term, no archive account or no connection
        Provider-->>Search: no results, without asking Paperless
    else
        loop until the page of results is full, for at most 4 pages of Paperless or 3 seconds
            Provider->>Client: term, the days of the date filter,<br>the page of 25 hits with the next hit
            Client->>Paperless: GET /api/documents/<br>?query=invoice&page=1<br>&page_size=25&fields=…<br>&created__date__gte=…,<br>with the token
            Paperless-->>Client: ID, title, date, correspondent,<br>type and excerpt of documents<br>412, 389, 371, …, and whether<br>a next page exists
            Provider->>Locator: the documents of the page,<br>user, archive account
            Locator-->>Provider: per document a file of the<br>archive account with its marker,<br>or none
            Provider->>Names: the correspondents and types<br>of the documents with a file
            Names->>Paperless: through the client, for the IDs<br>that the cache lacks: GET<br>/api/correspondents/?id__in=3,5<br>and /api/document_types/?id__in=1,2
            Paperless-->>Names: their names, which the cache<br>keeps for ten minutes
            Names-->>Provider: the names
        end
        Provider-->>Search: an entry for every document with a file, up to the limit: preview or icon, title, date, correspondent, type and excerpt, and the cursor of the next hit
    end
